==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|fro|en}} {{m|fro|curteis|}} (French {{m|fr|courtois}}), from {{m|fro|cort||court}}, displaced native {{w|Old English}} {{m|ang|hende||courteous, gracious, friendly}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|GenAm}} {{IPA|/ˈkɝti.əs/|lang=en}}
* {{a|RP}} {{IPA|/ˈkɜːti.əs/|lang=en}}
* {{audio|en-us-courteous.ogg|Audio (US)|lang=en}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# Showing [[regard]] or [[thought]] for others; especially, displaying good [[manners]] or [[etiquette]].
#: ''a '''courteous''' gentleman''
#: ''a '''courteous''' gesture''

====Synonyms====
* See also [[Thesaurus:polite]]

====Antonyms====
* {{l|en|discourteous}}

====Derived terms====
* {{l|en|courteously}}

